# clock — every site that renders a wall clock a human reads must place it in
# the reader's zone. Home Assistant reports timestamps in UTC.
#
# The surface is derived by internal/surfaceaudit.ClockSurface: any function
# containing a Go clock layout, or cutting an ISO timestamp on "T".
#
# This surface used to hold five renderers in four packages that disagreed with
# one another. It now holds three functions in internal/clock, because the fix
# for the disagreement was to delete the other implementations rather than to
# correct each of them — the shortest ledger is the one where the rule has only
# one place left to be wrong.
#
# The ceiling is the number of sites known to be unproven. It may fall without
# ceremony and may only rise by editing this line on purpose.
#ceiling 0

internal/clock/render.go:Short = proven: TestShortConvertsTheWireZone
internal/clock/render.go:ShortSeconds = proven: TestNaiveWireValueKeepsItsDigits

internal/cmd/log.go:systemLogToEntries = exempt: builds its value with time.Unix, which returns a Time already located in the reader's zone, so there is nothing to convert
internal/cmd/companion_logs_cmd.go:writeCompanionLogs = exempt: same shape, time.Unix over the companion's epoch seconds is already local

internal/clock/render.go:ShortColumn = proven: TestShortColumnIsUniformDownTheColumn
